00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:27.270
Now, to peel onions, the easy way,

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.980
I've got a whole bunch of these peels which actually...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:38.140
wanted to show you how you did it. Quickly, we'll say that this is a pan of boiling water. You just

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:43.440
take all your onions, put them in the water, and wait till the water comes back to the boil again,

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:51.710
and then leave them for about 20 seconds just to loosen the skin. Take them out, then peel them. And

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:59.970
when you peel them, we want to cook these holes. We want to leave just as much onion together.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.960
as possible. Now you see how that skin slips off. Now because we want them to

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:10.700
stay whole, you've got your root end here and you take your little knife and you

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.280
just pierce a little hole in that. Let's see how quickly that goes, but be

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:24.180
careful that you just shave off either end like that. There, now poke your little

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:28.920
hole in. Then there are peeled onions.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:37.610
and we're going to cook them in a pan like that you want to have a pan that will just hold them

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:41.860
you don't want them piled on top of each other then we put in a little bit of water

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:51.870
still till they're about half covered and we want some butter the butter adds flavor to them so we

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:57.100
about that about a tablespoon of butter like that and some salt

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.420
Then we want to bring them just to the simmer on top of the stove, and then you cover them.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.730
I don't have a cover. I'll use this and pretend we have one.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:14.840
You cover them, and you keep them in a very, very slow simmer for about 25 minutes until they're tender.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:20.420
Now, as we don't have 25 minutes, I've got some that have already been cooked.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:25.500
I cooked these last night, so you can see you can do this all ahead of time, and they're done when they're soft.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.710
But as you see, they've kept their shape.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:37.830
When they're done, then you just put them aside, and you can do them the night before if you want.

