if you were cooking the stew in the morning or even the night before you could have your mushrooms

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:23.640
ready and your onions ready and now our stew is cooked long enough so we're going to get it out of

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:24.120
the oven

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:36.310
is one that I've had in the oven for about three hours.

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:37.910
It's just about ready.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.300
Now this other one that we had in the oven

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:43.820
will take three hours more, so we'll just have to wait.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.660
Now comes the very important and not difficult thing

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.380
about making the sauce.

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:02.710
And what we're going to do here is just to,

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.140
the easiest way to de-grease the sauce

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.640
and to give it its finer, final flavoring

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:13.080
is just to pour the whole thing into a sauce pan.

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.060
We'll do here.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:18.150
I always find a towel awfully useful to have

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:20.960
hung around me, there.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:26.220
Then I'll let the sauce drain out,

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:27.950
and then we simply.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:41.320
stew back into the casserole there now we should have about two and a half to three cups of sauce

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:49.450
here which we do just about and what we do now is the final flavoring of it we also want to take

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:54.780
off any fat which is accumulated if you made this a day or two ahead of time you could put

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:59.970
it all in the icebox and then the fat would come up the surface and you scrape it off in this case

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.310
We're just going to skim it off the top.

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:05.640
Unless you're on one of those fat-free diets,

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.040
you want to leave a little bit in

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:09.220
because it gives a very good flavor.

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:12.810
Now we're going to taste it,

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.280
and it should be just exactly right at this point.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.510
Or if it isn't, we're going to make it.

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:26.100
So that's very good.

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.340
I think it needs a little more salt,

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:29.870
and it needs some pepper.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:40.320
You don't usually put the pepper into a sauce until just at the end because pepper sometimes can get a little bit bitter.

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:44.260
So this hasn't had any, so this is the pepper going in now.

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:48.880
Now I'll just taste it again to be sure.

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:55.980
Always remember to taste things because you can spend quite a bit of time and then forget to taste and find that it isn't just right.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:59.970
If you felt that it didn't have enough garlic, you could put some.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:07.310
in now so we could put in a little more tomato paste or a little more thyme in this case we're

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:14.620
fortunately find it's just right now for the thickening of it and this is a very simple

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:22.610
french thickening called a beurre mannier or a butter and flour paste we have about

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:29.370
say about three cups of sauce here so we want one tablespoon of flour per

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.730
cup of sauce and that'll give it just enough thickening and we just put the

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:42.920
flour into anything handy like a little bowl and then have softened butter

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:54.150
about it there and then we work the butter and the flour together and it

00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:59.600
makes what is called a paste and it's a very thickening it's not what you call a

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:08.140
cuisine thickening but it's what you always use for a stew like this very very typical of the

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:14.480
either the boeuf bourguignon or the coquivin there now that's in the paste we're going to take

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:20.730
the sauce off the simmer we'll put it on a burner which isn't going and just put this

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:24.480
flour paste in and beat it up.

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.250
These wire whips are often useful.

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:42.830
then we put it over heat again we want it to bring bring to the boil it just needs to boil

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:49.010
for about a second and while that's coming to the boil we put our braised onions in

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:53.220
and our sautéed mushrooms.

00:23:57.460 --> 00:23:59.380
Now that's boiled and you can see it's thick.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:03.500
What we wanted to do is just to be thick enough to enrobe the beef.

00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:08.260
And then, there we are.

00:24:15.670 --> 00:24:21.350
Now, if you want to do this ahead of time, you do it right to this point.

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:25.740
And then, when it's cool, you can cover it and refrigerate it.

00:24:25.820 --> 00:24:28.760
Be sure never to cover anything when it's hot.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:34.340
because it may sour that often happens you make a lovely chicken stew and then cover it up

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:39.210
and it turns sour just because you've covered it before it's cold but we're going to serve

00:24:39.210 --> 00:24:49.120
this right away so you want to heat it up just a little bit because you want the flavor of the

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:57.340
onions and the beef to all blend themselves with the stew that's going a little too hard so i'll

00:24:57.340 --> 00:24:58.320
put it at the side

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:06.490
In about two or three minutes, and if you had it in the icebox, you'd heat it up very slowly

00:25:06.490 --> 00:25:08.890
and baste the meat with the sauce.

00:25:10.420 --> 00:25:16.510
And then you'd cover it and simmer it very slowly for about two or three minutes

00:25:16.510 --> 00:25:19.260
until everything was tender and hot through.

00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:22.560
So we'll pretend we're doing that.

00:25:23.020 --> 00:25:25.700
You see that, the wonderful thing about this, so you say,

00:25:25.780 --> 00:25:27.960
Oh, I can't do anything that takes four hours.

00:25:28.220 --> 00:25:29.080
Oh, it's impossible.

00:25:29.350 --> 00:25:29.970
As you see,

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.560
you don't have to even look at it once it's in the oven.

00:25:32.560 --> 00:25:34.280
Once you've got the preliminaries done,

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:37.740
you can put it all together, put it away,

00:25:38.360 --> 00:25:40.320
or you can cook it the next time,

00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:43.200
and you can cook it the next day if you want.

00:25:43.920 --> 00:25:45.640
But it's just a lovely stew, and it's really,

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:49.940
it's a peasant dish, and peasants don't do

00:25:50.470 --> 00:25:53.450
simple hearty cooking, and that's just what this is.

00:25:53.790 --> 00:25:57.830
Well now this is ready to serve right now.

00:26:03.070 --> 00:26:07.770
This is going to be a very nice dinner that we have.

00:26:07.930 --> 00:26:10.290
We have our boeuf bourguignon,

00:26:10.790 --> 00:26:14.810
and we have what the French usually always serve with it,

00:26:14.950 --> 00:26:17.960
which are boiled potatoes with parsley on them,

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:21.250
and a very nice green salad of romaine,

00:26:21.860 --> 00:26:24.500
and as always, the usual French bread.

00:26:24.940 --> 00:26:27.000
You're gonna see French bread on all these meals

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.960
because the French always have bread at all of them.

00:26:29.460 --> 00:26:29.960
And...

00:26:30.280 --> 00:26:32.310
Also, we have a red wine.

00:26:32.490 --> 00:26:35.050
This is the same wine that we used for the cooking.

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:38.620
It's a domestic mountain red.

00:26:38.780 --> 00:26:40.040
It's a very nice wine.

00:26:40.310 --> 00:26:43.770
Or if you have lots of money, you can buy a fine burgundy,

00:26:43.870 --> 00:26:46.210
except with a beef stew like this,

00:26:46.330 --> 00:26:49.660
you don't use one of the terribly expensive burgundies.

00:26:49.950 --> 00:26:52.330
You use a young, full-bodied wine,

00:26:52.530 --> 00:26:55.410
because if you had a very old, delicate wine,

00:26:56.190 --> 00:26:58.910
the stew being very robust would kill the wine.

00:26:58.990 --> 00:26:59.970
And when you're serving wine,

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:06.790
you want to think of how it goes with the meal or how say how the beef and the wine marry because

00:27:06.880 --> 00:27:15.150
if this is robust the wine must be rather robust now next time we're going to do french onion soup

00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:22.160
gratinade it's one of the really great french soups and it's a it's fun to make and wonderful

00:27:22.160 --> 00:27:29.410
to eat and i hope that you will be with us and i hope also that you feel that you can make a good

00:27:29.410 --> 00:27:29.850
Do

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:39.320
after having seen this one is you remember you can use lamb chicken veal as well as beef and

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:45.470
it's all done exactly the same time same way it's only the cooking time that varies this took two or

00:27:45.470 --> 00:27:51.430
three hours chicken takes only about 30 minutes and you remember now how to saute mushrooms get

00:27:51.430 --> 00:27:57.580
the butter hot remember how the foam is supposed to look and don't crowd the pan don't crowd the

00:27:57.580 --> 00:27:59.480
pan either when you're making a beef

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.240
You're sauteing beef or you won't get it brown.

